opular of them all  gonosuba and tsukimichi are no exception  i think that it's an apt comparison yet  at the same time i think the tsukimichi  has a lot of merits that allow it to  stand out in its own right what are  those merits it's the way in which it  combines a lot of familiar tropes  channels meme energy in them like  konosuba and comes out as something  surprisingly refreshing and fun to watch  there's order in mayhem and this comedic  series just embodies that saying so well  it's a show with a lot of crazy moments  that captures the fun and appealing  aspects of several issachain if you're  intent on taking a break from the very  intense fights in power fantasies like  slime and you prefer something a bit  more chill and comedic then this could  be the isakai for you  for our next entry we take a look at  either den deities an old adage goes  that you shall not judge an anime by its  art alone yes the art makes a strong  impression and helps you tamper  expectations but we've got a lot of  hidden gems behind very simplistic  looking appearances anyone expected odd  taxi to take the world by storm how  about osama ranking in the action side  of things i'll gladly apply that to ida  denditis what i expected to be a very  quirky and light-hearted action comedy  ended up being one of my go-to shows for  unwinding it's got mapa at the helm and  it's from the same guy who brought us  the most cultured modern anime in  interspecies reviewers yep there's a lot  to like it's got violence edgy and all  that wild stuff that some of you who  like that more daring aspect of anime  would also like a pure fun and turn your  brains off show is what i'd normally say  but at the end of it all it'd be unfair  to just write it off as purely style  over substance  come on a gacha game anime doesn't have  any right to be this good but by god  they did it tactop destiny is the action  series that starts off in full throttle  and doesn't let go its premise seems to  be your ever